    "Two angles are supplementary. One measures 47°. What is the other?": "Supplementary angles add up to 180 degrees, so subtract the one you know from 180: 180 minus 47 is 133 degrees.",
    "A triangle has angles measuring 33° and 89°. What is the third angle?": "Every triangle's angles add up to 180 degrees. Subtract the two you know from 180: 180 minus 33 minus 89 is 58 degrees.",
