    "A right triangle has a hypotenuse of 15 and one leg of 9. What is the length of the other leg?": "Use the Pythagorean theorem, leg squared plus leg squared equals hypotenuse squared. The known leg squared is 81, and the hypotenuse squared is 225. Subtract to isolate the missing leg: 225 minus 81 is 144. The square root of 144 is 12, so that's the other leg.",
